{{!--
  Side-menu navigation tree (see GH issue #8), built from `.ids-list` /
  `.ids-list-item` (list/list.css, list/list-item.css) rather than fixtures —
  recurses over Antora's real `page.navigation` model.

  Depth conventions (see side-menu.css):
  - `data-depth` on each <ul> drives group bottom padding (24 for a group's
    own list, 12 / 8 for anything nested deeper — Figma's "Subpage" frames).
  - `.ids-list-item--tree--level-N` drives indentation. `--ids-list-item-
    tree-indent` is overridden to 8px (Figma's fixed nested-row indent)
    inside `.side-menu__nav`, rather than the DS default 12px/level.

  States are colour and weight only, never a background: the row renders
  `.ids-list-item` (layout, indent) plus this bundle's own `.side-menu__link`
  (cursor, focus ring, colour/weight per state) — deliberately without the
  DS's `--clickable`/`--selected` modifiers, which paint a background this
  design doesn't want. See side-menu.css for the four states (normal, hover,
  active/current, active+hover), all driven by `aria-current` and `:hover`.

  Expand/collapse is real ARIA (`aria-expanded`/`aria-controls`) on a plain
  toggle button beside the row — src/js/01-nav.ts drives it and everything
  server-renders expanded, so JavaScript-off degrades correctly per the
  issue's acceptance criteria.

  A parent entry with no `url` (a pure grouping node — Antora content
  structure, not this Figma frame, which shows no row for one) renders no
  row of its own: only its children, at the next depth. One that does have
  both a url and children is expandable.

  A LEAF entry with no `url` and no `items` either (Fumadocs' own
  `"---Label---"` category separator, preserved through the migration —
  see code/tools/fumadocs-migrate/build-nav.mjs) is different from a pure
  grouping node: it carries real `content` with nothing to descend into, so
  the two rules above would render it as nothing at all — silently losing
  Fumadocs' own section labels ("Getting started", "Build", ...) from the
  sidebar entirely. Rendered as its own non-interactive row instead: same
  `.ids-list-item` layout/indent as a real link, no `<a>` (nothing to
  navigate to), `.side-menu__link--label` in place of `.side-menu__link`
  for genuinely different states (see side-menu.css: no cursor, no hover/
  focus ring — there's nothing to click).
--}}
{{#if navigation.length}}
<ul class="ids-list side-menu__list" data-depth="{{or level 0}}">
  {{#each navigation}}
  {{#unless ./url}}
  {{#if ./items.length}}
  <li class="side-menu__item side-menu__item--group">
{{> nav-tree navigation=./items level=(increment ../level)}}
  </li>
  {{else}}
  {{#if ./content}}
  <li class="side-menu__item">
    <div class="side-menu__row">
      <span class="ids-list-item side-menu__link--label ids-list-item--tree--level-{{or ../level 0}}">
        <span class="ids-list-item__text"><span class="ids-list-item__label">{{{./content}}}</span></span>
      </span>
    </div>
  </li>
  {{/if}}
  {{/if}}
  {{else}}
  <li class="side-menu__item{{#if ./items.length}} side-menu__item--branch{{/if}}">
    <div class="side-menu__row">
      <a class="ids-list-item side-menu__link ids-list-item--tree--level-{{or ../level 0}}"
        href="
          {{~#if (eq ./urlType 'internal')}}{{{relativize ./url}}}
          {{~else}}{{{./url}}}{{~/if}}"
        {{~#if (eq ./url @root.page.url)}} aria-current="page"{{/if~}}>
        <span class="ids-list-item__text"><span class="ids-list-item__label">{{{./content}}}</span></span>
      </a>
      {{#if ./items.length}}
      <button class="side-menu__toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-label="Toggle {{detag ./content}}">
        {{icon "arrows" "chevron-down-outlined"}}
      </button>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
{{> nav-tree navigation=./items level=(increment ../level)}}
  </li>
  {{/unless}}
  {{/each}}
</ul>
{{/if}}
